<title>UK: UK Labour legally confident on windfall tax - Blair.</title>
<headline>UK Labour legally confident on windfall tax - Blair.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Labour Party is confident it will be able legally to introduce a windfall tax on privatised utility companies, leader Tony Blair said on Sunday.</p>
<p>Commenting on newspaper reports that the tax would be open to legal challenge, he said in a BBC television interview: &quot;We have had legal advice on this which is very, very clear indeed.&quot;</p>
<p>He added that there was &quot;a very well organised lobbying campaign&quot; against the tax by both the firms likely to be affected and by the ruling Conservative Party.</p>
<p>Blair declined to say how much would be raised from the tax, but confirmed it would be used to help people under 25 into work or training.</p>
<p>== London Newsroom +44 171 5427950</p>
